<commit message="Refactor: add iterator helpers for scene/item lookup

Add _get_scene(), _iter_building_items(), _iter_belt_items(), and
_iter_room_items_for_room() to centralize the 'do it in room or document'
branching logic. Refactored sync_* and refresh_* methods to use these
iterators, making the code much cleaner and less repetitive."/>

Done! Added iterator helpers that centralize the branching logic:

- `_get_scene(scene_room_id)` - get Scene for a room_id or document
- `_iter_building_items(building_id, scene_room_id)` - iterate all visual items for a building
- `_iter_belt_items(belt_id, scene_room_id)` - iterate all visual items for a belt  
- `_iter_room_items_for_room(room_id)` - iterate all RoomItems displaying a room

Now the sync methods are much cleaner - they just iterate and apply operations without branching.
